Third-party provenance
======================

Rhombus/HOL is a direct Rhombus reimplementation of the HOL Light proof
engine and standard theories. The future surface language will be implemented
with native Rhombus macros; literal theory quotations are expanded offline.
Private type-inference algorithms support the original Metis reconstruction.
HOL Light's parser and printer are translated as well (`parser.rhm`,
`printer.rhm`).

HOL Light
---------

The engine modules under `rhombus/hol/` are direct or algorithm-preserving
translations of HOL Light sources, principally:

- fusion.ml -> fusion.rhm
- basics.ml -> basics.rhm
- nets.ml -> nets.rhm
- equal.ml -> equal.rhm
- bool.ml -> bool.rhm
- drule.ml -> drule.rhm
- tactics.ml -> tactics.rhm
- itab.ml -> itab.rhm
- simp.ml -> simp.rhm

The additional standard theory modules from theorems.ml through define.ml
retain their original module names. Generated headers retain original author
notices. The pinned HOL Light source revision is
`cba9198db76e9dfb89cbd653df9412d01f65b22a`. The HOL Light copyright and
BSD-2-Clause terms are retained in `THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES/HOL-Light.txt`.

HOL Light Boyer-Moore library
-----------------------------

`rhombus/hol/Boyer_Moore/` translates HOL Light's `Boyer_Moore/` directory
at the same pinned revision (the waterfall prover of Papapanagiotou and
Fleuriot, "The Boyer-Moore Waterfall Model Revisited", arXiv:1808.03810).
Its notice reads: (c) University of Edinburgh, University of Cambridge, INRIA
1994; (c) Petros Papapanagiotou & Jacques Fleuriot, University of Edinburgh
2007-2017; distributed under the same license as HOL Light (BSD-2-Clause).
The code builds on R. J. Boulton's HOL88 Boyer-Moore automation. Each
translated file keeps its original header.

OCaml
-----

`rhombus/hol/private/ocaml.rhm` reproduces the relevant OCaml 4.14.1 runtime
hashing behavior needed by the finite partial functions of `lib.rhm`, and
preserves OCaml's random generator. Map.Make and
Set.Make instances used by the standard theories translate the original AVL
algorithms. `rhombus/hol/private/format.rhm` translates OCaml 4.14.1's
`stdlib/format.ml` (the pretty-printing engine the printer runs on).
`tools/ml2rhm/stdlib/` carries OCaml 4.14.1's `map.ml` and `set.ml`
unchanged, with their COPYRIGHT and LGPL-2.1 terms; the translator expands
Map.Make and Set.Make from them. Their OCaml license terms are retained below.

The OCaml 4.14.1 LGPL-2.1 terms and linking exception are retained in
`THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES/OCaml.txt`.

